{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1791389000000-architect-d15-signoff-astra.gpt-6-astra.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"I found two blockers: exclusive holders’ reply and progress journals are backed only by memory atoms, and the host loops still end shutdown based solely on the endpoint server. That leaves process-crash recovery unsupported and can skip custody cleanup when no server exists or it stops first.\n\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-08 05:38:10 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-08 12:38:10 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nCHANGES — (1) **Provide actual crash-recoverable holder storage.** `compose.cljc:123` creates memory-backed journals; `holder-media` at line 367 uses them for both replies and progress, while `restart` at line 486 depends on the surviving composition and its atoms. A file-backed authority does not make these journals durable. Supply reopenable reply/progress backends and stable recovery configuration, and pin reconstruction without the original composition, handles or atoms—including a read-before-retention crash and a pending release. (2) **Make shutdown draining independent of the endpoint server.** JVM `main.cljc:1140` skips draining without a server; Node/Dart likewise enter their drains only through `server'` branches at lines 1314/1442. All three also terminate when the server stops, regardless of custody cleanup. Enter the bounded drain when custody requires cleanup, continue custody ticks after endpoint completion, and test absent/already-stopped servers plus releases blocked until a later tick and throughout the budget. (3) **Enforce the composition stop latch for subsequently added holders.** `add-holder` at `compose.cljc:436` installs an unstopped driver into an already-stopped composition, and `program-step` at line 618 ignores the composition latch. Reject additions after stop or stop newly added drivers, and make composition-level program stepping a no-op after stop; pin both `holder` and `source`. These violate the production-recovery and shutdown contracts despite the reported green suites. The disclosed store-audit allowlist entry is justified: its three maps carry the content-store configuration, not guest-store mutations. Read-only review; no suites run.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
